==Sanskrit==

===Alternative scripts===
{{sa-alt|फल}}

===Etymology===
{{unknown|sa|Uncertain}}. The original meaning was "fruit". It is commonly considered a borrowing from {{bor|sa|dra-pro|*paẓam|t=ripe fruit}} (compare {{cog|ta|பழம்}}, {{cog|ml|പഴം}}, {{cog|te|పండు}} and {{cog|kn|ಹಣ್ಣು}}). However, Mayrhofer says nothing speaks for that and instead groups it with the family of words derived from the root {{m|sa|फल्#Etimology_2|फल्|to burst, split}} (as ripe fruit is prone to burst, see {{l|sa|फल#Related_terms|related terms}} for other words related to "bursting, splitting"). It might derive from {{der|sa|ine-pro|*bʰel-|*(s)bʰel-|to swell}} (with [[w:S-mobile]]). In this case the Dravidian words are from Sanskrit.<ref>{{R:inc:EWAia|vol=2|pages=201-2}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
{{sa-IPA|a=1}}

===Noun===
{{sa-noun|g=m}}

# {{c|sa|Dogbane family plants}} {{vern|coral swirl}} ({{taxlink|Wrightia antidysenterica|species}})
#: {{syn|sa|काही|शनपर्णी|गिरिमल्लिका|कौटज|वृक्षक|शक्रपादप|सङ्ग्राहिन्|वत्सक|वरतिक्त|कुटज|शक्रपर्याय|कोहिन्|शक्र|भद्रज|वत्साह्वय|तिक्त|महागन्ध|कौट|शक्रवृक्ष|वृक्ष|कूटज|प्रावृषेण्य|कलिङ्ग|प्रावृष्य|कालिङ्गक|यवफल|पाण्डुरद्रुम|कालिङ्ग}}

